    "text": "In the arrangement shown in the diagram, pulleys are small and springs are ideal.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>are force constants of the springs and mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>. If the time period of small vertical oscillations of the block of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mtext>x&nbsp;seconds</mtext></math>,&nbsp;then find the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0024376_Question_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 228px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext><mtext>eq</mtext></msub></mfrac></msqrt></math><br /><br />where&nbsp;&nbsp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext><mtext>eq</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4&nbsp;</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mtext><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">k</mtext><mn>4</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">T</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msqrt><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mtext><msub><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">K</mtext><mtext>eq</mtext></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mtext>x</mtext></math><br /><br />So,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <msqrt> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>0</mn> <mo>/</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>6</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </msqrt> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> <mtext>,&nbsp;</mtext> <mtext>x</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </math>",
